  "gainNote": "playbackGainDb is applied by offbeat-audio.js at playback. Each clip moves two-thirds of the way toward -20 LUFS, so quiet places stay quieter than loud ones, capped so the decoded true peak never exceeds -3 dBTP (room for two clips overlapping in a crossfade). maxGainDb is that cap. limiterDb marks clips whose loudest transients were reduced by up to that many dB with a lookahead limiter before encoding, to make room for the boost. Edit playbackGainDb to taste; the module never applies more than maxGainDb."
